'suboss' is a C shell script which can be used to submit
a BOSS job.
Now it is possible to give command line options.
E.g., to perform a geometry optimization using Z-matrix file
'test.zmat' and parameter file 'test.par', you could say simply

% suboss CALC=opt test
or
% suboss CALC=opt test.zmat

For scripting purposes, suboss uses . extensions for file names.
INFILE, UPFILE, SAVE, AVERAGE, ZMATRIX, SLVZMAT, PARAMETER,
SUMMARY, OUTPUT, and PLTFILE have .in, .up, .save, .ave, .zmat, .slvzmat,
.par, .sum, .out, and .plt extensions, respectively.
Input file names are supposed to have this extension scheme.
Below is the output of 'suboss -help'.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Description: suboss.csh is a C shell script for submitting a BOSS job.
Usage: suboss.csh -h
       suboss.csh -help       --- Print help message

       suboss.csh [VAR1=VAL1 VAR2=VAL2 ...] [filename[.zmat]]

    Valid VAR names are listed below. (no spaces around '=')
      BOSS  --- path of BOSS executable (default=/usr/local/bin/BOSS)
      LIB   --- diretory where BOSS library files (org1box,org2box,watbox,
                oplsaa.sb) reside (default=/usr/local/lib/boss)

      MXCON --- A positive integer (default=200000)
                Max configuration if CALC=bgn_equ,cont_equ,bgn_ave, or cont_ave
                Max optimization cycle if CALC=opt
                Atom number for the chosen dihedral if CALC=dihed
                Max tries for conformational searching if CALC=search
                Ignored when CALC = "freq".
      NRUN  --- Total number of BOSS runs. (default=5)
                Meaningful only when CALC=MC
      CALC  --- A type of calculation to perform. Valid values are
                bgn_equ  --- begin equilibration of MC simulation. (default)
                cont_equ --- continue equilibration of MC simulation.
                bgn_ave  --- begin averaging of MC simulation.
                cont_ave --- continue averaging of MC simulation.
                opt      --- geometry optimization.
                dihed    --- dihedral angle driving.
                freq     --- frequency calculation.
                search   --- conformational searching.
      NEWRUN -- 0 or 1
                1 = Begin a new conformational searching (default)
                0 = Restart a previous conformational search
      RC0   --- Reaction coord for the reference solute     (default=0.5)
      RC1   --- Reaction coord for the 1st perturbed solute (default=0.0)
      RC2   --- Reaction coord for the 2nd perturbed solute (default=1.0)

      SENDMAIL -- 0 or 1 (default=1)
                1 = Send e-mail upon completion of a job
                0 = Do not send e-mail upon completion of a job

Examples:
(In all examples, it is assumed that parameter file 'test.par'
 already exists in the same directory where 'test.zmat' resides.)

1. to begin equilibration using Z-matrix 'test.zmat' with total max
   configurations of 20000*5 and RC0, RC1, RC3 of 0.1, 0.0, and 0.2,
  % suboss.csh CALC=bgn_equ MXCON=20000 NRUN=5 RC0=0.1 RC1=0.0 RC2=0.2 test.zmat

2. to continue equilibration of the previous run (mentioned above),
  % suboss.csh CALC=cont_equ MXCON=200000 NRUN=10 RC0=0.1 RC1=0.0 RC2=0.2 test.zmat

3. to begin an averaging of the previously equilibrated system,
  % suboss.csh CALC=bgn_ave MXCON=200000 NRUN=10 RC0=0.1 RC1=0.0 RC2=0.2 test.zmat

4. to optimize a geometry using Z-matrix 'test.zmat' without getting e-mail,
  % suboss.csh CALC=opt SENDMAIL=0 test.zmat

5. to calculate frequencies using Z-matrix 'test.zmat',
  % suboss.csh CALC=freq test.zmat

6. to perform a conformational search using Z-matrix 'test.zmat',
  % suboss.csh CALC=search MXCON=1000 test.zmat

7. to restart a previous conformational search,
  % suboss.csh CALC=search MXCON=1000 NEWRUN=0 test.zmat

8. to use your own BOSS executable (e.g., /home/lim/boss/BOSS),
  % suboss.csh CALC=opt BOSS=/home/lim/boss/BOSS test.zmat

